// madc --mcp with the madcgit module loaded (split arc 1C.14): -lmadcgit
// (.flags) brings the version history to the server's tools — graph.status
// answers this file's git state and the versioned layer, graph.commits the
// commits touching it, graph.revision refuses a revision git cannot resolve,
// and tools/list carries the history tools. Asserted by SHAPE over the
// repository the test runs in (every lane runs the suite from a checkout
// root) — never a sha, a branch or a count history would move. ORACLE: git
// rev-parse's refusal of an unknown revision; the MCP specification
// 2025-06-18 for the envelopes (isError content for a tool's own refusal).

long add(long a, long b)
{
    return a + b;
}

int main(void)
{
    return (int)add(2, 3) - 5;
}
